622 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 361 0 R
/E (For each codebook entry, the model keeps track of two moving statistics: how often that entry is selected, and the average encoder output assigned to it. Instead of updating the codebook directly with noisy gradient steps, the embedding is updated using a smoothed average of the encoder vectors that choose it. In simple terms, each codebook entry gradually moves toward the group of latent vectors it represents.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
