635 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 362 0 R
/E (The smoothing term prevents unstable updates when a codebook entry is rarely selected or not selected at all. This helps avoid division-by-zero issues and keeps rare entries numerically stable. In addition, some implementations reset dead codebook entries by replacing them with random encoder vectors when they are used too rarely. This reset strategy can help reduce codebook collapse, but it is only a practical heuristic and does not guarantee that all codebook entries will be used equally.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
